Peter Stern <peter@wiscpa.weizmann.ac.il>

>> The DPW series comes in three flavors, i for Intel, a for Alpha (and
>> thus the "AlphaBIOS", version 5.33) and au for Alpha Unix (as you
>> already guessed).  The i series can run either W95 or WNT, the a series
>> just WindowsNT and the au series either WindowsNT or DU.  As I
>> understand it, the a-series is priced considerably lower than the
>> au-series (~$3000 less?) because it is missing some hardware necessary
>> to run DU and you aren't paying for the DU license.  So I don't think
>> that you can do what you want to do.  Of course, if what you have is a
>> DPW 500au with WindowsNT installed, you should be able to boot from DU.

My PWS500 is indeed a PWS500au. That's what the SRM finally said.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
rye <rye@jtasc.acom.mil>

>> If you have the SRM console installed (Licensed) then it is very simple.
>> Enter setup mode from the Alpha Bios Screen  (F2)
>> Enter Advanced Setup (F6)
>> Tab down to the Console Type and change it to Digital Unix
>> Press F10 twice (Saves Settings)
>> Power Cycle the system
>> Should be running SRM

To be more exact :
        - Enter setup mode from the Alpha Bios Screen  (F2)
        - Enter the CMOS setup menu
        - Enter Advanced Setup (F6)
        - Tab down to the Console Type and change it to Digital Unix
        - Press F10 twice (Saves Settings)
        - Power Cycle the system
And it runs SRM the next time.

That's the answer.

