From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Jan 24 02:29:28 1998
From: Jim Griffin <griffin () vol ! com>
Date: Sat, 24 Jan 1998 02:29:28 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Telnet/FTP from Alpha
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078654411033

In an earlier query, I had asked about the inability to telnet and ftp 
from an Alpha running DU 4.0B to an Encore system running the proprietary 
MPX operating system.  A SunOS 4.1.x system was able to connect to the 
Encore, but not the Alpha.  A packet sniffer reported that the difference 
in IP headers was that the Alpha was setting the Do Not Fragment flag.

At the suggestion of a VMS user (the query was also posted to 
comp.sys.dec), the problem was probably in the MTU Discovery area.

I found that by setting the pmtu_enable parameter in the inet area using 
dxkerneltuner to zero fixed the problem.  dxkerneltuner is used to modify 
kernel parameters, immediately and/or at boot time.

Thanks for the responses.

BTW - I have Solaris 2.6 and SGI Irix 6.x systems with the same basic 
problem [more accurately, the Encore has the problem, but I can't patch 
it :(  ].  DU is the only OS I've found yet that allows this particular 
kernel mod.



Jim Griffin - TNS/AANR
