Subject: Printing to AS400
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078654410823


     Hi Managers,
     
     I am trying to print from Digital UNIX 4.0B 4100 Servers to the 
     printers on AS400, but with no success. The reports that I am trying 
     to print are plain ascii files. I also tried with converting the file 
     to EBCDIC and then print it on the AS400, but with no luck. Seems like 
     the AS400 needs the file with all attributes. How do I do turn the 
     attributes and what attributes to make it work? How do I make AS400 
     happy :(
     
     Here's what happening "I think"...
     When the AS400 receives a spool file from another AS400 it comes with 
     all the attributes defined. A job on the receiving AS400 receives the 
     file and retrieves all the attributes and creates the spool file. When 
     the spool file is received from a non AS400 system and tries to 
     retrieve the attributes and doesn't find any, it then plugs in some 
     default values. Since the AS400 plugs in its own values for the file 
     name and user they are always going to be the same. The only 
     difference is the User Data field which is the file name coming from 
     the Unix side. If we are going to do bulk printing for Unix the AS400 
     needs to read these attributes to determine font size and 
     distribution. 
     
     Report Manager can key in on User Data only. The problem is the Unix 
     file name is not always going to be the same for the same report. The 
     spool file comes formatted from Unix in ASCII. The AS400 can only read 
     EBCDIC and there for can not use filters to search for data within a 
     report.
     
     I have talked to IBM and they basically told me the same thing. When 
     we send a spool file from the AS400 to another AS400 and want to send 
     all the  spool file attributes we turn on a flag (*alldata). We would 
     need to do something similar on the Unix side to send all attributes. 
     
     At this point the only solution I can think of is to look for some 3rd 
     party software that might do this. I don't know if any exist. 
     
     Anyone ran into similar situation? High volume printing from UNIX to 
     AS400. Your help and comments are appreciated. 
     
     Thanks,
     Ronny Eliahu
     
     The Walt Disney Company 
     Disney World Wide Services
     Disney Studio, Burbank California

