From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Jan 12 14:38:43 1998
From: Dick Abraham <abrahad () gov ! on ! ca>
Date: Mon, 12 Jan 1998 14:38:43 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMM: More than 3 advfs volumes. Risky?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078654410757


I received numerous responses to my question:

  The manual page for the addvol command indicates that more than 3
  volumes in an advfs domain can be risky even though up to 250 volumes
  is supported.


The answers I recieved were numerous and all indicated that the reason more
than 3 volumes can be risky is that if one physical volume in a domain fails
all data in the domain is lost and it it statistically more likely that
one of 3 volumes will fail than only one volume and even more likely that
one of 4 volumes will fail than one of 3 volumes.


Thanks to all who responded, your help is very much appreciated.

I am going with 4 volumes but realize I must be even more vigilant about
backups than I was before.

Richard

